        <div class="row">
            
       <div class="col-lg-8">
             <img class="blog-hero-image" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Institute of Banking Personnel Selection PO Notification 2026 Apply Online">
             <div class="blog-content">
                 <div class="blog-body">
                    <h1 class="blog-title text-center mb-4">IBPS PO Notification 2026: Your Guide to Applying Online and Acing the Exam!</h1>
                    <p class="lead mb-4">Aspiring to a prestigious career as a Probationary Officer (PO) in India's public sector banks? The Institute of Banking Personnel Selection (IBPS) PO Notification 2026 is a golden opportunity you won't want to miss. With exam dates already announced, it's time to gear up for the highly competitive selection process. This comprehensive guide provides all the crucial details you need, from application procedures to eligibility criteria and exam patterns.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Key Dates for IBPS PO 2026 Recruitment</h2>
                    <p>The IBPS has already released its calendar for 2026-27, marking out the crucial dates for the PO examination. Mark these in your calendar and plan your preparation strategically!</p>
                    <table>
                      <thead>
                        <tr>
                          <th>Event</th>
                          <th>Tentative Dates</th>
                        </tr>
                      </thead>
                      <tbody>
                        <tr>
                          <td>IBPS PO Notification Release</td>
                          <td>June 2026</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                          <td>Online Application Window</td>
                          <td>June - July 2026 (Post-notification release)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                          <td>IBPS PO Prelims Exam</td>
                          <td>August 22nd &amp; 23rd, 2026</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                          <td>IBPS PO Mains Exam</td>
                          <td>October 4th, 2026</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                          <td>Interviews</td>
                          <td>November 2026 (Expected)</td>
                        </tr>
                      </tbody>
                    </table>
                    <p class="highlight-text">The official notification, expected in June 2026, will provide complete details on vacancies, application fees, and other important aspects of the CRP-XVI PO/MT recruitment drive.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Who Can Apply? IBPS PO Eligibility Criteria 2026</h2>
                    <p>Meeting the eligibility requirements is the first step towards your banking career. Thousands of applications are rejected each year due to eligibility errors, so pay close attention.</p>

                    <div class="benefit-card">
                      <p>✅ <strong>Nationality:</strong> Candidates must be a Citizen of India, or a subject of Nepal/Bhutan, a Tibetan Refugee, or a Person of Indian Origin (PIO) who has migrated from specific countries with the intention of permanent settlement in India.</p>
                      <p>✅ <strong>Age Limit:</strong> As of the specified cut-off date (to be confirmed in the official notification, but generally around July 1st/August 1st of the application year), candidates should be between 20 and 30 years old. Age relaxation is applicable for reserved categories (e.g., 3 years for OBC, 5 years for SC/ST, 10 years for PwBD).</p>
                      <p>✅ <strong>Educational Qualification:</strong> A Bachelor's Degree in any discipline from a University recognized by the Government of India or an equivalent qualification is mandatory. Crucially, you must possess a valid mark-sheet/degree certificate stating that you are a graduate on the day you register for the exam, and the final result of your graduation must be declared on or before the last date of registration.</p>
                      <p>✅ <strong>Computer Literacy:</strong> Basic computer knowledge is required. Some sources mention a valid Certificate/Diploma/Degree in computer operations/language, or demonstrated proficiency in computer operations.</p>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">The Online Application Process: Step-by-Step</h2>
                    <p>The application for IBPS PO 2026 will be conducted entirely online through the official IBPS website (www.ibps.in). It is crucial to follow the steps meticulously to avoid rejection.</p>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">1. New Registration</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">Visit the official IBPS website (ibps.in) and click on the "CRP PO/MT" section. Look for the link to apply online for CRP-PO/MT-XVI (or the relevant year's recruitment) and then select "CLICK HERE FOR NEW REGISTRATION". Provide basic details like your name, mobile number, and a valid email ID. A provisional registration number and password will be generated and sent to your registered email and mobile number.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">2. Upload Scanned Documents</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">You will need to upload scanned images of your photograph, signature, left thumb impression, and a handwritten declaration as per the specified guidelines (size and format). Ensure your signature is not in capital letters and your thumb impression is clear. The handwritten declaration text must be in your own handwriting and in English.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">3. Fill in Detailed Application Form</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">Proceed to fill out the detailed application form with your personal, educational, and category-specific information. Be precise and accurate as changes may not be allowed after final submission.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">4. Preview and Validate</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">Before final submission, use the preview option to thoroughly review all the details entered and documents uploaded. This is your chance to correct any discrepancies.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">5. Pay Application Fee</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">Pay the application fee online through debit cards, credit cards, internet banking, IMPS, or mobile wallets. The application fee is INR 850 for General and OBC categories, and INR 175 for SC/ST/PWBD candidates.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">6. Final Submission and Print</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">After successful payment, submit your application. It is highly recommended to print out the e-receipt and the submitted application form for your records.</div>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">IBPS PO 2026 Selection Process: The Three Tiers</h2>
                    <p>The IBPS PO recruitment is a three-stage process, designed to assess candidates comprehensively.</p>
                    <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ <strong>Preliminary Examination:</strong> This is an online objective test, primarily a qualifying round. Scores from this stage do not contribute to the final merit list.</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Main Examination:</strong> Candidates who clear the Prelims proceed to the Mains. This online exam consists of both objective and descriptive tests. Scores from the Mains exam are crucial for the final selection.</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Interview:</strong> Shortlisted candidates from the Mains exam are called for a face-to-face interview, which carries a maximum of 100 marks. This is the final stage of selection.</p>
                    </div>
                    <p>The final merit list is prepared based on a combined score from the Mains Examination and the Interview, typically in an 80:20 ratio respectively.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Exam Pattern and Syllabus Highlights</h2>
                    <p>Understanding the exam structure is key to effective preparation.</p>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">IBPS PO Prelims Exam Pattern 2026</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">
                        <p>The Prelims exam is 60 minutes long, with 100 objective multiple-choice questions for 100 marks.</p>
                        <table>
                          <thead>
                            <tr>
                              <th>Section</th>
                              <th>No. of Questions</th>
                              <th>Max Marks</th>
                              <th>Duration</th>
                            </tr>
                          </thead>
                          <tbody>
                            <tr>
                              <td>English Language</td>
                              <td>30</td>
                              <td>30</td>
                              <td>20 minutes</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                              <td>Quantitative Aptitude</td>
                              <td>35</td>
                              <td>35</td>
                              <td>20 minutes</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                              <td>Reasoning Ability</td>
                              <td>35</td>
                              <td>35</td>
                              <td>20 minutes</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                              <td><strong>Total</strong></td>
                              <td><strong>100</strong></td>
                              <td><strong>100</strong></td>
                              <td><strong>60 minutes</strong></td>
                            </tr>
                          </tbody>
                        </table>
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">IBPS PO Mains Exam Pattern 2026</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">
                        <p>The Mains exam is more comprehensive, including both objective and descriptive sections.</p>
                        <table>
                          <thead>
                            <tr>
                              <th>Section</th>
                              <th>No. of Questions</th>
                              <th>Max Marks</th>
                              <th>Duration</th>
                            </tr>
                          </thead>
                          <tbody>
                            <tr>
                              <td>Reasoning &amp; Computer Aptitude</td>
                              <td>45</td>
                              <td>60</td>
                              <td>60 minutes</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                              <td>General/Economy/Banking Awareness</td>
                              <td>40</td>
                              <td>40</td>
                              <td>35 minutes</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                              <td>English Language</td>
                              <td>35</td>
                              <td>40</td>
                              <td>40 minutes</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                              <td>Data Analysis &amp; Interpretation</td>
                              <td>35</td>
                              <td>60</td>
                              <td>45 minutes</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                              <td>Descriptive Test (English: Essay &amp; Letter Writing)</td>
                              <td>2</td>
                              <td>25</td>
                              <td>30 minutes</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                              <td><strong>Total (Objective)</strong></td>
                              <td><strong>155</strong></td>
                              <td><strong>200</strong></td>
                              <td><strong>160 minutes</strong></td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                              <td><strong>Grand Total</strong></td>
                              <td><strong>157</strong></td>
                              <td><strong>225</strong></td>
                              <td><strong>190 minutes</strong></td>
                            </tr>
                          </tbody>
                        </table>
                        <p>There is a penalty of 0.25 marks for each incorrect answer in the objective tests of both Prelims and Mains.</p>
                        <p>For a detailed syllabus breakdown for each section, candidates are advised to refer to the official IBPS PO 2026 notification once released. However, common topics include Puzzles, Seating Arrangement, Syllogism, Data Interpretation, Simplification, Current Affairs, Banking Awareness, Reading Comprehension, and Error Spotting.</p>
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="cta-section">
                        <h3>Start Your Preparation Today!</h3>
                        <p>With the IBPS PO 2026 exam dates announced, now is the perfect time to intensify your preparation. Stay tuned to the official IBPS website for the detailed notification in June 2026 and take the first step towards a fulfilling career in the banking sector!</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
       </div>
    
            
            
